> It may be possible to support introspection for the other backends by checking if the text field has a constraint with IS JSON or JSON_VALID().

@pope1ni 
It seems that obtaining the `CHECK` constraint information would require another query (or modifying the existing query for some backends). I think that needs to be implemented first, in a separate PR. I don't know about the best way to do that, though, since I'm not very familiar with introspection.

@laymonage @felixxm Do you think it's possible that `REGEXP BINARY` doesn't work also with MySQL 5.7? https://github.com/django/django/pull/10065/files

Maybe it would be better to replace

    if self.connection.mysql_version < (8, 0, 0):

with

    if self.connection.mysql_version < (5, 7, 0):

in `regex_lookup` function as `REGEXP_LIKE` is in MySQL 5.7?
